# Servo sweep
# Level 3 - Sensors and motors
#
# A servo motor turns slowly from one side to the other and back.
# You learn: 'use' to add a library, angles in degrees and smooth moves with over:.
# You need: a small servo (such as an SG90): signal (orange) to pin 9, red to 5V, brown to GND.
# Bigger servos need their own power supply - the board's 5V can't feed them.

board uno
use mujard.servo

arm = Servo(pin 9)

task sweep:
    while true:
        arm.move(180 deg, over: 2 s)   # move() also works in the background...
        wait 2 s                       # ...so wait until it has arrived
        arm.move(0 deg, over: 2 s)
        wait 2 s
